### Prerequisite: `netlify dev` running locally, and a `gh_token` value obtained by completing
### the flow in github-auth-callback.http (or copied from DevTools → Application → Cookies
### after logging in through the app).
### Uses the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8888/.netlify/functions
@ghToken = paste-gh_token-cookie-value-here
@owner = your-github-username
@repo = your-test-repo
@path = stations.json

### F-4/F-5: reads a file via the Contents API using owner/repo/path exactly as given.
### Expect the proxied GitHub response body, and no gh_token value anywhere in it.
GET {{baseUrl}}/github-api-proxy?owner={{owner}}&repo={{repo}}&path={{path}}
Cookie: gh_token={{ghToken}}

### Read without a token cookie — expect 401 { "error": "Not authenticated" }.
GET {{baseUrl}}/github-api-proxy?owner={{owner}}&repo={{repo}}&path={{path}}

### Write (create/update) — include `sha` (from the read response above) when updating an
### existing file; omit it to create a new file.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/github-api-proxy
Cookie: gh_token={{ghToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "owner": "{{owner}}",
  "repo": "{{repo}}",
  "path": "{{path}}",
  "message": "test: update stations.json via github-api-proxy.http",
  "content": "eyJzdGF0aW9ucyI6W10sImRlZmF1bHRGdWVsIjoiU1A5NSJ9"
}
